<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>A ship at <m>(20^\circ\,\mathrm{S}, 42^\circ\,\mathrm{E})</m> sails due east along its parallel at <m>{15}</m> knots for <m>{36}</m> hours.</p><p>(a) Find the distance sailed.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans1"/> nm  </p><p>(b) Find the change in longitude, in degrees correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans2"/> <m>^\circ</m>  </p><p>(c) Find the new longitude, in degrees correct to 1 decimal place.</p><p><fillin characters="8" name="ans3"/> <m>^\circ</m> [ E | W ]  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Distance <m>=</m> speed <m>\times</m> time <m>= {15} \times {36} = {540}</m> nm.</p><p>(b) On the parallel <m>{20}^\circ</m>, one degree of longitude is <m>60\cos {20}^\circ</m> nm long, so the change in longitude is</p><p><me>\frac{ {540} }{60 \cos {20}^\circ} = {9.578} \approx {9.6}^\circ.</me></p><p>(c) The ship sails east, so an east longitude increases and a west one decreases. New longitude: <m>{51.6}^\circ\,\mathrm{E}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>540</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>9.57759995228</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>51.5775999523</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p>E</p></answer>
</stack-static>